{
  "requirement": "TBV automatically redacts recognized credentials in source excerpts delivered\nby its inspection tools and in node text supplied to its agent requests.\nThe built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with redaction markers\nwhile preserving line breaks. SDK-supplied outline languages use the same redacted\nregions, so changing only a recognized credential does not change its\nstructural fingerprint.\n\nLoaded source snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans;\nredaction applies when preparing model-visible text and structural hashes.\nFilesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record. Applications supply\ntheir own answer values and remain responsible for what those answers contain.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`, and the tests that cover each:\n\n1. **Source excerpts from inspection tools are redacted.**\n   - `src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` runs `search_text` and `search_structure` on a file with a GitHub token and a multi-line RSA private key. It asserts the exact redacted excerpt, that the token and key body lines are absent from the serialized output, and that the file on disk is unchanged. It also asserts that the dependency fingerprint comes from the original text.\n   - `src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[child_headers_use_redacted_source_when_the_language_supplies_a_header]` covers `read_node` child headers. It asserts the header shows `[REDACTED:GitHub Token]` and the raw token is absent.\n2. **Node text supplied to agent requests is redacted.**\n   - `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery]` checks every request's chat history, covering both queued contents and the `read_node` tool result. It also asserts the dependency fingerprint holds the original text.\n   - The tool's source view shows the `secret` literal as the marker string, which looks like the tool's own redaction of a token literal. I took the test's intent from its name and assertions.\n3. **Secret regions are replaced by markers and line breaks are preserved.**\n   - `src/redaction/tests.rs#fn[private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines]` and `fn[tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code]` check the marker output and surrounding code.\n   - `fn[regions_extend_both_ways_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte]` checks CRLF handling, region extension and a large input.\n   - `fn[slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole]` checks slices against the whole.\n   - `fn[heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted]` and `fn[configuration_keys_do_not_add_sdk_specific_secret_rules]` check that only recognized credentials are redacted.\n   - Line-count preservation is also asserted in `src/outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[redaction_never_changes_an_outline]`.\n4. **SDK outline languages use the same redacted regions, so a credential-only change leaves the structural fingerprint alone.**\n   - `src/outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values]` covers Rust, Markdown and text. It also checks that a change outside the credential still changes the hash.\n   - `fn[redaction_never_changes_an_outline]` covers YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and text outlines.\n   - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]` checks an SDK-supplied unknown-language file: the fingerprints are equal for different tokens, and `format()` is redacted.\n5. **Loaded snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans.** The same `tests/outline_content.rs` test asserts `contents.text() == source`, and that the selected node's `text()` still contains the token while its `format()` is redacted.\n6. **Filesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record.** `tests/storage.rs#fn[storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text]` stores a record whose output contains a token-shaped string. It asserts the loaded output equals the original and the raw token is present in the file on disk.\n7. **Applications remain responsible for their own answers.** This is a statement of responsibility, not a testable obligation.\n\nI found no obligation that is untested, no wrong expected result and no weak assertion.",
